{"agent":"bg43","data":{"by":"bg43","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"For a full-suite item run (`full=True`, `for_item=True`, `override=False`), `_plan` enters the `if for_item and not override:` branch and returns `scope = CS.plan(cfg, tree, base, requested=\"full\")`. The function’s own contract in this diff says a full-suite run keeps “no planned scope”; the condition should also exclude `full` (`if for_item and not full and not override:`). As written, a full-suite item run gets an explicitly planned full scope instead of `None`, so callers can treat the full command as a planned/selected-scope run, contrary to the expected full-suite behavior.","digest":"0335340bed7b0eed","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_plan","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_plan"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`lock_wait` is the suite-slot wait limit (it is passed directly as `wait_s` to `SL.hold`), while `budget` is the execution budget passed later to `_execute`. The line `budget = max(1, int(lock_wait) - int(waited))` therefore overwrites the command’s real budget with the remaining wait allowance. Concretely, if a run has a normal 600s command budget and a 30s per-run suite-wait override, and the slot is acquired almost immediately, `_execute` is called with `budget=30`, so a legitimate suite that would have been allowed 600s is killed at 30s.","digest":"49d5695545f0fc26","location":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_run_under_slot","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/ci/runner.py:_run_under_slot"}],"diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"output_digest":"a8222546cfa0c837","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-ci-merge-tree-stale-after-queue-wait.critic.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261107T212708Z-d6301628.jsonl","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1,3],"status":"PARTIAL","terminated_by":"SIGTERM","tree_sha":"a07c0c6631fd+clean"},"gate":"critic","reason":"the review was terminated by SIGTERM mid-round after 2 chunk(s) we